    "what-changed-text": {
      "type": "Text",
      "props": {
        "text": "AEON broke out, gaining 46.3% in 24h on 2.1× average daily volume — clearing both BREAKOUT thresholds. Liquidity in the aeon/WETH pool grew 32.7% to $1.01M ($248.4K added) as price climbed. Whale activity was two-sided: the largest single trade was a $5.94K sell at $0.0000130 (16:42 UTC yesterday), followed by two buys — $3.06K at $0.0000152 (05:58 UTC) and $2.96K at $0.0000151 (21:30 UTC) — as buyers absorbed the early sell pressure and pushed price higher through the session. Buy/sell ratio eased slightly to 1.18 from yesterday's 1.39, but volume more than doubling the weekly average confirms this wasn't a thin-book move.",
        "variant": "body"
      }
    },
